# Scratch, backup and duplicate files — never belong in the repo
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
*.tmp
*~
* copy.*
* copy [0-9].*

# Runtime media served from the services' static mounts.
#
# The generated upload trees are NOT ignored any more (see the note at the end
# of this block). What must never be committed from here is a REAL guest's
# document: only the seeded SPECIMEN assets belong in this tree.
#
# This rule used to say `.../static/uploads/`, which matches nothing -- the
# real directories are upload_image/, users/, identity_proofs/ and
# room_incidents/. So 112 generated files were committed, and because each
# re-seed mints new filenames they matched exactly one developer's database
# and were orphans in every other clone. Worse, a guest identity document
# uploaded while testing would have been committed too.
#
# The images that are meant to be in the repo:
#   Backend/tools/seed/photos/     vendored source photographs, the seed input
#   Backend/db/<release>/uploads/  a release export, restored by
#                                  Backend/tools/restore_uploads.py
#
# CHANGED 2026-09-28: the per-service upload tree below is now TRACKED, at the
# repository owner's request, so a clone carries the imagery a fresh install
# displays. The trade-off the rule above was written to avoid is real and still
# applies: every re-seed mints new UUID filenames
# (Backend/tools/seed/images.py), so these files are tied to the database they
# were generated beside. Committing them does NOT make them portable -- for a
# release that has to match a specific database, use Backend/tools/export_release.py
# and Backend/db/<release>/uploads/ instead, which is the path the release notes
# and Backend/db/*/README.md already describe. A real guest's identity document
# must never reach this tree: it is for the seeded SPECIMEN assets only.
# Backend/Services/*/templates/static/

# Standalone nested repo, not part of this project
/hotelerp.in/

# Pre-reseed database backups. A local safety net written by hand before
# running Backend/tools/seed_demo_data.py --confirm; it contains the data the
# rebuild replaced, so it must never be committed over the top of the release.
backups/
# Raw originals downloaded by the seed photo fetcher. Reproducible, large,
# and not the cropped files that actually ship.
Backend/tools/seed/_photo_cache/
